  "definition": "Astrobiology studies the origin, evolution and distribution of life in the Universe. It connects biology and chemistry with geology, astronomy and planetary science: how life began on Earth, which conditions allow it to persist, how living systems alter their surroundings, and how those effects might be recognised elsewhere.[^1] No life beyond Earth has been confirmed.",
